{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfefEatknPgzfSBvu8bos","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 04 is done. The dataset is defined, deduplicated, written, independently checked and priced, and the write-up is `paper2/dataset.md`. The gate passes (lake build ok, one `sorry` as allowed, MOSP pytest 1,379 passed, pathwidth_solver pytest 114 passed). The split run's log has no `!!!` line.\n\n**What the dataset is**\n- **Size:** 21,754 instance files from 20 collections (every collection in `benchmarks/README.md` §1 plus the MOSP corpus) reduce to **17,714 isomorphism classes**. They were deduplicated by nauty certificate across collections and across problems.\n- **Duplicates removed:** the MOSP corpus comes out at 3,667 classes, the same figure as before. Rome goes from 11,534 files to 11,199 classes, the VSPLIB trees from 50 to 28, and the control-flow graphs from 1,817 to 1,070.\n- **Unread graphs:** 78 PACE graphs over 5,000 vertices are matched by file content only, not up to isomorphism.\n- **Values:** 16,087 classes have a certified pathwidth with a witness layout, and 862 more have a witnessed upper bound only.\n- **Format:** one JSON line per class. Each holds the graph, width, provenance, evidence, the witness layout, the value under each of the nine exactly-equivalent problems, and every member with its map onto the representative graph. Bound-certified records also carry a minor certificate as the lower-bound proof.\n\n**The independent check**\n- `paper2/dataset_check.py` uses only the standard library and imports nothing from the repository; 15 tests cover it and the builder.\n- With `--sources` it reports **0 failures on 16,949 records**. Every bound certificate replays, and all 20,987 member files are re-read with the checker's own readers and mapped onto their record.\n- Refutation-certified values (12,552 records) cannot be checked from the record; they rest on the repaired search until item 05 gives them a proof object.\n\n**Against published values**\n- All 84 Small graphs agree with Mallach (2018).\n- 10 of the 11 VLSI circuits certify at their published best-known track counts; W4 is still open at 28 against 27.\n- All 11 certified Carvalho & Soma values agree with the published spreadsheet. One of our upper bounds is better than the published best: Random-200-200-6-7 at 119 against 120.\n\n**Orientation finding**\n- Carvalho & Soma's files list customers as rows, unlike the Chu & Stuckey files in the same repository. My first pass read them the wrong way round. The comparison against published values caught it (one instance certified at 127 against a published 124), and the 150 instances were rerun.\n- Our Chu & Stuckey reading is confirmed against all 40 published class means.\n- The Frinhani large set's orientation is still unsettled: the published densities point both ways. None of its values is certified, so nothing rests on it yet.\n\n**Run and price**\n- **This item's run:** 5.7 core-hours on 4 workers, of which 1.2 went on the wrongly oriented first pass.\n- **Graph sets:** one more budget step for every open graph within the C engine costs at most about 500 core-hours. On the Rome record, each such step closes only about 40% of what it attempts.\n- **MOSP corpus:** the last five values are each priced in the hundreds of core-hours.\n- **Out of reach:** most of Carvalho & Soma (all but the dense class), Frinhani, and the 154 classes above 1,024 vertices. The cost model is used there well beyond the sizes it was tested on, and the write-up says so.\n\n**One thing for item 07:** `Random-125-125-2-4_0` was re-certified by the split run at 02:55 today, unchanged, after 154 core-hours. `solver_fix.md` still says \"partial\", which is out of date rather than wrong. It is recorded in PROGRESS.md for item 07 to update; three instances remain in flight.\n\n**Left open:** one Rome witness that did not come back within 120 s, the licences, the four data requests, and the runs beyond this item's budget. Everything is uncommitted, as instructed. About 21 MB of new data sits under `paper2/data/dataset/`, which is not git-ignored, so the driver's commit will include it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1072,"cache_read_input_tokens":292719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1072,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75542546-c9f7-4da7-b4e0-5f724162e16f","uuid":"42aa0a9c-156d-41bf-9b69-ab64bcb4dd82","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:19:01.135Z","request_id":"req_011CfefEaWSQ9DHZChwXpQma"}
